#use libc
#use io

// Regression test for the FFI NUL-termination safety seam: Dva Strings are
// NUL-reserved by construction (the byte data[len] == 0), but the reservation
// is a runtime property of the *whole* string. A view s(a..b) (C10) shares the
// parent's buffer, so its data[len] is whatever byte follows in the parent —
// which is not necessarily NUL. Passing such a view to a C function expecting
// NUL-terminated char* (atoi) without a copy would make the C callee read past
// the view's end. codegen must detect data[len] != 0 at the call site and hand
// C a temporary NUL-terminated copy instead.
//
// The canary: parent holds "123459\0", but the view covers only "12345", so
// view.data[5] is the digit '9' (57), not NUL. atoi on the raw buffer would
// consume "123459" and return 123459. Only the copy path (a clean "12345\0")
// yields exactly 12345.

parent = "123459"
v = parent(0..5)

n = libc::atoi $ v
io::out $ n